{"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"commandExecution","id":"call_F83fuazq5mBCs8XGb0SCDv4D","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -c 'git diff -- kernel/src/device/serial.rs kernel/src/main.rs kernel/tests/panic_serial.rs'","cwd":"/Users/egv/dev/PaperDOS/.yolo-runner/clones/bd-976e.1","processId":"16531","status":"completed","commandActions":[{"type":"unknown","command":"git diff -- kernel/src/device/serial.rs kernel/src/main.rs kernel/tests/panic_serial.rs"}],"aggregatedOutput":"diff --git a/kernel/src/device/serial.rs b/kernel/src/device/serial.rs\nindex 488433b..9be1a1b 100644\n--- a/kernel/src/device/serial.rs\n+++ b/kernel/src/device/serial.rs\n@@ -27,6 +27,31 @@ pub fn serial_write_fmt(args: fmt::Arguments<'_>) {\n     let _ = SerialWriter.write_fmt(args);\n }\n \n+/// Emit a deterministic panic report to the serial console.\n+///\n+/// The output format is stable and line-oriented:\n+/// - `!!! PANIC !!!`\n+/// - `LOC:<file>:<line>:<column>` (or `LOC:<unknown>`)\n+/// - `MSG:<message>`\n+pub fn serial_write_panic_report(location: Option<(&str, u32, u32)>, message: fmt::Arguments<'_>) {\n+    serial_write_bytes(b\"\\r\\n!!! PANIC !!!\\r\\n\");\n+    match location {\n+        Some((file, line, column)) => {\n+            serial_write_fmt(format_args!(\"LOC:{}:{}:{}\\r\\n\", file, line, column));\n+        }\n+        None => serial_write_bytes(b\"LOC:<unknown>\\r\\n\"),\n+    }\n+    serial_write_fmt(format_args!(\"MSG:{}\\r\\n\", message));\n+}\n+\n+/// Format a panic using [`core::panic::PanicInfo`] and emit it to serial.\n+pub fn serial_write_panic_info(info: &core::panic::PanicInfo<'_>) {\n+    let location = info\n+        .location()\n+        .map(|loc| (loc.file(), loc.line(), loc.column()));\n+    serial_write_panic_report(location, format_args!(\"{}\", info.message()));\n+}\n+\n /// Register the byte-write callback for the serial console.\n ///\n /// # Safety\ndiff --git a/kernel/src/main.rs b/kernel/src/main.rs\nindex 5498cfb..308cdc9 100644\n--- a/kernel/src/main.rs\n+++ b/kernel/src/main.rs\n@@ -33,7 +33,9 @@ mod device {\n     use kernel::boot_app::{load_and_run, JumpMode};\n     use kernel::device::display::X4DisplayTransport;\n     use kernel::device::raw_gpio::RawOutputPin;\n-    use kernel::device::serial::{serial_write_bytes, serial_write_fmt, set_serial_write_fn};\n+    use kernel::device::serial::{\n+        serial_write_bytes, serial_write_panic_info, set_serial_write_fn,\n+    };\n     use kernel::device::storage::{RuntimeSdFs, SdSpiDevice};\n     use kernel::display::ssd1677::{\n         emit_addressing_init_block, emit_power_init_block, emit_reset_preamble,\n@@ -433,8 +435,7 @@ mod device {\n \n     #[panic_handler]\n     fn panic(info: &core::panic::PanicInfo<'_>) -> ! {\n-        serial_write_bytes(b\"\\r\\n!!! PANIC !!!\\r\\n\");\n-        serial_write_fmt(format_args!(\"{}\\r\\n\", info));\n+        serial_write_panic_info(info);\n         loop {\n             spin_loop();\n         }\n","exitCode":0,"durationMs":0},"threadId":"019d5442-09af-7ba0-9081-56c96a87ed6b","turnId":"019d5442-09b2-76d1-b68b-88d956769067"}}
